## <%if .DisplayName%><%.DisplayName%><%else%><%.Slug%><%end%> — shape: a bot with a public contract (ADR-099).
##
## The contract is the face the outside reads without opening the prompts:
## what the bot takes, what it produces, the file it delivers, the checks a
## reader can run on those, and the effects it has. It is declared ONCE, at
## top level, named by the workflow's `contract:`, and the compiler holds it
## to THIS program — a contract the program contradicts is a compile error,
## never a display: an input is a declared var of the same type, required
## exactly when the var has no default (C300); an output names the node and
## field that produce it, of the field's type (C301); a criterion names a
## port and a registered evaluator with its parameters (C302). `iterion
## validate` renders the bound contract (and returns it as `public_contract`
## with --json), and holds the bundle's other readers to it: the manifest's
## launch face (C254) and a parent `subbot`'s `with:` (C255). A criterion is
## declared and held for shape here — nothing evaluates it at run time yet —
## so the goal check the contract declares is ENFORCED by the deterministic
## entry gate below. `goal` carries the scaffold's empty default (every var
## of the form has one), so to the contract it is optional: a parent
## `subbot` is not held to pass it (C255 holds required inputs only) and the
## gate is what refuses an empty goal. Fill in: the mission, `goal`.
## docs/dsl.md (§ The public contract) · docs/adr/099-public-contracts.md

dsl: 2

<%template "vars_block" .%>
schema check_out:
  configured: bool

schema report:
  summary: string
  done: bool

prompt mission:
<%indent 2 .Instructions%>

prompt work_user:
  Carry out the mission for the goal below. Report a one-paragraph summary
  of what you did, and whether the goal is fully done.

  Goal: {{vars.goal}}

## The entry gate, deterministic and before any LLM call: no goal, no run.
## `!!` is the expression language's truthiness — trimmed and lower-cased,
## an empty or blank goal is refused with a typed code, and so are the
## words false, no and 0 (stricter than the contract's min_length, which
## counts characters untrimmed and admits a blank goal and those words
## alike).
compute check:
  output: check_out
  expr:
    configured: "!!vars.goal"

## The work: one agent with a typed output, PUBLISHED as a versioned
## artifact of the run (`publish:`). The contract names a field of it
## (`from: work.summary`) and, through a file port, the node alone
## (`from: work`) — which is what makes the artifact the bot's delivered
## file.
agent work:<%template "llm_fields" .%>
  system: mission
  user: work_user
  output: report
  publish: report

fail goal_unset:
  description: "no goal was given"
  code: GOAL_UNSET
  message: "goal is empty: say what this run works on"

## The public face. Every port mirrors the program: `goal` repeats
## `vars.goal` (its type, its requiredness, its default — a port may repeat
## what the var says, never contradict it); each output names its producer.
## A file port carries a `file:` block (media type, size floor, schema) and
## names a node that publishes. Effects document what the bot does to the
## world; they grant nothing — the sandbox and the permission gate keep the
## admission.
contract public:
<%- if .DisplayName%>
  display_name: <%quote .DisplayName%>
<%- end%>
<%- if .Description%>
  responsibility: <%quote .Description%>
<%- end%>
  version: 1
  inputs:
    goal: string
      description: "What this run works on — refused empty at entry (GOAL_UNSET); optional to the contract only because the scaffold gives every var a default"
  outputs:
    summary: string
      description: "One paragraph on what was done"
      from: work.summary
    done: bool
      description: "Whether the goal is fully done"
      from: work.done
    report: json
      description: "The work's published output, a versioned artifact of the run"
      file:
        media_type: "application/json"
        schema: report
      from: work
  criteria:
    goal_is_not_empty:
      kind: min_length
      port: input.goal
      params: {min: 1}
    summary_is_not_empty:
      kind: min_length
      port: output.summary
      params: {min: 1}
  effects:
    reads_the_workspace:
      description: "Reads the repository it runs in; its only product is the run's published report"
    spends_llm_budget:
      description: "One agent call per run"
      paid: true

workflow <%.WorkflowName%>:
  contract: public
  entry: check
<%- if .Worktree%>
  ## Isolate the run in a git worktree; the report is an artifact of the
  ## run, so nothing of it depends on the checkout.
  worktree: auto<%else%>
  ## In place: the bot reads the workspace and writes nothing to it — its
  ## product is the published report, an artifact of the run, not a
  ## commit. `worktree:` unset means `auto`, so the opt-out is written.
  worktree: none<%end%><%template "dials" .%><%template "budget_block" .%>
  check -> goal_unset when not configured
  check -> work when configured
  work -> done
